        "input": {
          "level": "preferred",
          "summary": "Replace mandatory ICC arbitration (seat Osaka or New York) with exclusive jurisdiction of the state and federal courts in New York County, subject only to temporary injunctive relief elsewhere; New York governing law in Section 18.3 is unchanged.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] New York law already governs under Section 18.3, but our playbook requires courts rather than mandatory arbitration, and the current seat mechanic can place a Dispute in Osaka. We have therefore replaced the ICC arbitration forum and its tribunal machinery with exclusive jurisdiction of the state and federal courts in New York County, preserving each Party's ability to seek temporary injunctive relief elsewhere and retaining the internal-counsel privilege protection.",
